"author_id": "59184587158", "id": "18135556378639066", "text": "@johnleavitt bruhhhh", "timestamp": 1792800865, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "hakbodi", "author_id": "59184587158", "id": "18210167824366815", "text": "How is everyone in this comment section so dense??? This tool never claimed to preserve the composition, it just removes the most featureless pixels when scaling the image. Adobe made headlines a few years ago for coming up with exactly thus tech and now we get to use it for free.", "timestamp": 1792800836, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "nebular_inkstain", "author_id": "28102102292", "id": "17965921397980828", "text": "we implemented this in comp sci bachelors. It\u2019s an elegant algorithm", "timestamp": 1792418877, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "charcharliee_", "author_id": "43276038", "id": "18180099844448946", "text": "bu the mountain changes shape. if you compare it to real life, if the painting is a view irl then it wont match. literally this image is the easiest to do in photoshop", "timestamp": 1792372363, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "therrell.cello", "author_id": "47582513315", "id": "18103721063562900", "text": "Ever heard of Ma?", "timestamp": 1792348027, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "kovbasyukpavel", "author_id": "291456886", "id": "17973208368153337", "text": "It can be used as transition FX, smth like Dolly zoom. Also reminds me parallax a little", "timestamp": 1792319501, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "sam_n.j", "author_id": "1435380070", "id": "18339493756256561", "text": "Mountain in the back gets surprisingly destroyed and now is the focus point because its so jagged", "timestamp": 1792307555, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "alex.w.benj", "author_id": "27706996730", "id": "18060198662799155", "text": "This deeply upsets me please get a new image", "timestamp": 1792202682, "like_count": 0}, {"author": "sebblz", "author_id": "28083468", "id": "18157761919507809", "text": "Peep show voice over", "timestamp": 1792177989, "like_count": 0}], "we